I haven't been nethacking for a long time now, but started again a few
weeks ago, and now I've ascended, of all things, a tourist(!).

I didn't expect this tourist to make it... he was the last in a rather
long line of botched protection racket attempts. He was just really,
really lucky in the initial game. Kiapat started out trying to do the
protection racket, only to accidentally kill one too many floating
eyes, twice too often (including a few other things), and so ended up
with Exp:3 by the time he got to Minetown (grotto version). Unlike his
predecessors, he got lucky in that none of the levels before Minetown
were dark, so that made things a lot easier. After using a 100zm item
for, um, a business venture, he managed to earn enough money to get
down to about AC:6 or so. Found some good dwarvish mithril early on,
which gave him AC:0 by the time he reached Minetown, which helped a
LOT.

Then he started back to the main dungeon, and found on Dlvl:6, one
level below the Oracle, the stairs to Sokoban, and TWO altars, one
co-aligned, one not. So he did the sacrifice thing, did Sokoban, found
a BoH which was badly needed at the time, and pretty soon got
Magicbane from the altars (obviously, the non-coaliagned altar didn't
stay that way for very long).

Then he decided to take a tour down to Minebottom, and amassed quite a
collection of potions and gems and other such items. He was still only
about Exp:8 or so at this time. Anyway, pretty soon he identified the
luckstone, and started carrying it around. Around this time, he
managed to get to about AC:-3.

And then begins the slow descent into the depths of the dungeon. Got
caught once robbing a vault, and used a ?oEarth to keep the guard at
bay (and there he remains to this day, in a tunnel leading into the
vault). Found a cursed magic lamp early on, and saved it as a
permanent light source. Also, begin to slowly switch to more
spell-friendly equipment (he had swindled enough shops and vaults by
this time that switching from mithril to studded leather armor was not
a big setback). Pretty soon, Kiapat had learned how to cast simple
spells.

Kiapat soon hit the Quest level, but got scared off when he saw
demiliches in the first level, even before he got to talk to
Twoflower. In any case, he was only Exp:12 at this point, so he
resumed dungeon diving. Found a Big Room, and much hilarity ensued
when he cut a long worm into 4 pieces, and filled up 30% of the Big
Room with them ("The long worm bites itself!").

He kept diving, and by good luck, hit Fort Ludios. He had acquired a
ring of conflict by this point, and put that to good use. Pretty soon,
he had amassed great wealth, and got to intrinsic AC:0 from the
minetown priest. Around this time, while dipping potions in a fountain
in the Oracle, a water demon suddenly decided to grant him a wish. So
he acquires a nice shiny +2 suit of black dragon scalemail, and
fireproof waterwalking boots from another blessed magic lamp he found.
Around this time, one of his many short-lived pets stepped into a ^oPM
and turned into yellow fungus, which remains there to this day. He has
not had the heart to end its miserable existence since.

With this, and also with teleport control/teleportitis acquired from
tengus, he finally reached Exp:14 and headed off to the Quest. Turns
out that he never needed to fight the demilich; a quick reflex to put
that skeleton key to good use took care of the problem. So he worked
his way through the different towns until he finally tracked down the
Master of Thieves. Of course, having first taken the precaution to
block off the up stairs with a ?oEarth, the Master was pretty much
mince meat when matched against Kiapat's teleporting abilities. A few
zaps of a /oFire later, the PYEC was his.

So he goes back to his stash at Dlvl:6, and prepared himself to go
down to Medusa, who was found sleeping down at Dlvl:28 or so. The
castle was immediately below, and Kiapat had a lot of fun squishing
monsters with the drawbridge using wizard lock and knock. Coupled with
=oConflict, the castle was pretty soon cleared out, and he saved the
WoW for later use. Somewhere along the way, he had acquired a nice
shiny helmet of brilliance, and so, after sorting out his loot, he was
down to AC:-20 or so. By this time, he had acquired a dangerous
collection of daggers for throwing purposes, and after collecting
enough of them, he rustproofed them and enchanted them to +3 or so.

With this, he went down to the Valley and beyond, and decided that he
really didn't want to take a long time, so he never bothered to
explore Gehennom thoroughly. He spent all of his ?oMM trying to speed
up the process, and got through Asmo and 'Zeeb by bribing, and Juiblex
was neutralized in short order with said +3 daggers. He had to take a
detour in the middle to go back to Dlvl:6 (using c?oTP) to unload all
the juicy goodies he was acquiring, as well as try to donate more
money to the Minetown temple, but didn't get any more AC improvement.
Around this time, he decided to stop picking up loot and to finish off
the game soon. He had gotten down to AC:-30 by this time, and about
350 maxhp from alchemy. So going back to Gehennom, he worked his way
down to the bottom, stoning Orcie with a rubber chicken, and
attempting several times to acquire pets from the purple worm species.
Unfortunately, none of them were long-lived, either getting slain by
angry mobs or stumbling into ^oPM and turning into less useful forms.
Kiapat decided to move on, and found Vlad's Tower around the same
place as Rodney Tower. Then he found the vibrating square, and left
the bell on it.

So back to Dlvl:6 he went, stuffing all his gems in a spare BoH, and
digging out straight paths from stairs to stairs on every level, and
left his ascension kit next to the stairs on Dlvl:1. Sorting out his
massive loot on Dlvl:6, he used up two wishes on magic markers, and so
he now has AC:-45, and his Vorpal Blade has been honed to +5, and his
collection of dangerous daggers to +6. With more alchemy, he got
himself to a whopping 470+ maxhp. With this, he headed down to
Rodney's, having amassed about 4 /oDeath. =oConflict cleared out the
zoo pretty quickly, and using a rubber chicken, he neutralized almost
all of Rodney's minions, only to find, to his dismay, that it rotted
away just before he had a chance to hit Rodney with it. Undeterred, he
pulled out the /oD's and soon, the Book was his.

So down he went to the Sanctum, having messed up the Invocation
sequence at least once to his own embarrassment. Rodney appeared and
got /oD'd. He engraved the E word with Magicbane a few times just to
sort through the hordes in a timely manner. Soon, he had found the way
into the inner temple, and nailed the high priest to the wall with his
daggers. Then, grabbing the Amulet, he made good use of the !oGL which
he had cursed for this occasion, and so left the slobbering hordes
behind for good. The mysterious force seemed to be on vacation for the
first 4-5 levels or so, and then it woke up and gave our tourist many
setbacks, including several more occasions for Rodney to get zapped
with /oD. But when he finally made it to Juiblex's swamp, he got
totally fed up with this whole force thing, and quaffed the other 6
!oGL which he had also prepareed for this purpose. And it so happened
that 6 was precisely the number he needed to get one level above
Medusa's.

So he worked his way up to Dlvl:6, and dropped off a few items no
longer deemed necessary (he left them at the stash, no less, for
completely sentimental reasons), and made his way up to the BoH at
Dlvl:1. Somewhere along the way, a disenchanter damaged his helmet, so
before he left for the Plane of Earth, he locked himself in a room dug
out by his trusty old pickaxe (while Rodney was raging outside!),
wished for another magic marker, and got his helmet to +5 (AC:-47).
Then he kicked the door open, and Rodney was instantly upon him,
trying to ToD him. Luckily, it failed, and luckily, the room was so
small that the /oD bounced and dispatched Rodney. Of course, Rodney
appeared again as soon as our tourist visited the Plane of Earth, and
was dispatched with for good with another zap of the /oD.

Using c?oGD, Kiapat made it through Earth and Air quickly. The dreaded
air elementals were still pretty nasty, even at AC:-47 (!!), so he
resorted to /oD to dispatch them quickly. The c?oGD didn't do as well
in Fire, 'cos too many actual gold piles were lying around, but
luckily, the portal was close by, so our tourist found it rather
quickly. Water was a lot more tricky, though. Using c?oGD didn't help
that much, because the portal kept moving around. Eventually he wrote
an uncursed ?oGD and read it after !oConfusion instead, but then a
corpse covered the portal over so he couldn't see it. After another
eternity, he finally stumbled upon it, and so ended up on Astral.

He decided to face Famine first, having amassed a gigantic collection
of K-rations earlier on (of which he could only afford to bring about
10 to prevent getting burdened---he had a pile of about 40+ which
were blessed, and 30+ which hadn't been blessed; turns out that
wasn't necessary). Oddly enough, this altar was the right one,
although none of the denizens appeared to be scared when he stepped in
(why?).

And so, the story of our tourist ends here. This is my first tourist
ascension, and I must say, it's actually a relatively EASY class to
play, once you've survived the first part of the game. The PYEC made
wands and rings very useful. I didn't even get that many favors from
praying (only did that twice on the altar: the second time was a
crowning, which made it pretty much pointless from then on). Magicbane
saves a LOT of headache with Rodney randomly cursing stuff. Even
though I made the mistake of improving short sword to Expert and
didn't even use a short sword in the end, the daggers pretty much make
up for it (killing a dragon with 5 or 6 daggers is pretty handy, esp.
if you throw 3 at a time). The genociding of h's was really an
afterthought, after an unfortunate encounter with an MMF and
forgetting many important items.

Oh yes, and the tourist never parted with his trusty old camera from
the beginning of the game. He is currently looking for a Kodak store
in the Astral Plane... :-)

